## For loop
For loops are very simmilar to while loops: The syntax is:
```ts
for (start; stop; step) {
    code
}
```
Start is the variable initilized when you start the loop, stop is just like a while loop, that is the condition for the loop to execute, and step is what happens on each run.
```ts
for (let i = 0; i < 15; i++) {
    code;
}
```
Is equivelant to:
```ts
let i: number = 0;
while (i < 15) {
    i++;
    code;
}
```
So much slimmer, right!
Us at MeTube realized out previous solution was inneficient: replace it with a for loop.

